      "problem": "Suppose $n=8r+12,$ where $r\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even.\n\nThe number $n$ is even since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =8r+12 \\\\  & =2({{field-1}}) \\\\  & ={{field-2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=$ {{field-3}}, which is an integer.",
